# Preserve line endings EXACTLY as committed.
#
# This is a fork of upstream (tonikelope/megabasterd), which ships MIXED line
# endings -- many files are CRLF, some are LF, each matching upstream per-file.
# Any automatic normalization (e.g. `* text=auto`) would flip files to LF and
# cause a conflict against upstream on every future merge.
#
# `-text` disables ALL end-of-line conversion, so files are stored and checked
# out byte-for-byte no matter what anyone's core.autocrlf is set to. It does NOT
# renormalize existing files (unlike text/text=auto), so adding this file causes
# zero churn. Real text files still diff normally -- Git auto-detects text vs
# binary for diffs independently of the `text` attribute.
#
# See CLAUDE.md "Upstream-merge hygiene". Do NOT change this to text=auto.
* -text

# Be explicit about binaries so Git never attempts text diffs or merges on them
# (`binary` is shorthand for `-diff -merge -text`).
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.jar   binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
